s Fionn's enemy. He rescued Fionn from three powerful hags in a cave at Keshcorran. Fionn gave him a daughter to marry and once let him rest by the Shannon. Yet enmity finally ruled. Fionn killed Goll after his own freedom. Goll then lived 30 days without food or water at the edge of Ireland. Mac Smaile of the Fianna killed him. Some legends say he found a home on the western islands. People sometimes confuse him with King Balor, who had one killing eye.", "okr": {"objective": "Recount Goll mac Morna as the one-eyed rival of Fionn bound in an endless feud.", "key_results": ["Goll was born Aed and lost an eye in combat, gaining the name one-eyed.", "His struggle set Clan Morna against Clan Baíscne.", "He rescued Fionn from hags at Keshcorran before enmity returned.", "Fionn killed him, and Mac Smaile of the Fianna finished the deed."], "evidence": "Monaghan 2008, s.v. 'Goll mac Morna' (citing MacNeill, The Festival of Lughnasa, 1982)."}}
